      "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4BKoLG",
      "body": "Adding a data point, since this thread and #517 touch on whether an inactive SIM is enough.\n\n**Setup:** Orbic RC400L (`device = \"orbic\"`), running a custom build based on Rayhunter 0.13.0 with local changes (not a stock release), Verizon SIM (home PLMN 311-480) that was activated in the past and then deactivated when I cancelled the plan.\n\n**What I see:** the modem never talks to a tower while Rayhunter is recording, so only the broadcast-based heuristics have anything to work with.\n\n- About 20 hours of recordings contain only SIB1 / SystemInformation and Paging. There are zero RRC connection requests and zero NAS messages.\n- The \"No NAS messages seen in 5 minutes, SIM possibly not working\" warning fires 5 minutes into every recording.\n- Signal is not the problem: Verizon cells are received at up to about -55 dBm.\n\n**Modem state over AT (`/dev/smd8`):**\n\n    AT+CPIN?     +CPIN: READY\n    AT+CEREG?    +CEREG: 0,0\n    AT+COPS?     +COPS: 2\n    AT+CGATT?    +CGATT: 0\n    AT+CEER      +CEER: EMM attach failed\n    AT^SYSINFO   ^SYSINFO: 1,0,1,9,1\n    AT+COPS=0    +CME ERROR: SIM failure\n\n**Things I tried:**\n\n- `AT+CFUN=4` then `AT+CFUN=1`: no attach attempt appeared in the capture.\n- Full reboot: Rayhunter started recording about 23 seconds after power-on. I checked roughly the first 100 seconds of that recording and it shows no attach attempt. `AT+CEER` already reported \"EMM attach failed\" about two minutes after boot, so my guess is the modem tries once in those first seconds and is rejected before Rayhunter is listening. I could not confirm that.\n\nThis looks like the same behaviour @Tunas1337 described in #517 (one attach attempt, a reject, then nothing until reboot), except that here the single attempt is never captured.\n\n**Why it matters:** with a SIM in this state, the heuristics that need a connection (IMSI requested, null cipher, 2G redirect on release) can never fire. The heuristics doc already says most heuristics depend on signaling with the core network, but the FAQ says an inactive SIM \"is sufficient ... to detect cell towers and potential IMSI catchers\", which reads as full coverage.\n\nTwo suggestions:\n\n1. Have the FAQ say that an inactive SIM may leave only the broadcast-based heuristics working, and that a persistent \"No NAS messages\" warning is the sign of this.\n2. Is there any way to see the attach attempt that happens at boot, before the daemon starts recording? Without it there is no way to tell which reject cause the SIM is getting.\n\nHappy to run more AT commands if that would help.\n",
      "author": {
        "login": "AlienMajik",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118037572?u=8570f9242f1d0cca86d4037ae50c441b2751d6e2&v=4",
        "url": "https://github.com/AlienMajik"
